      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Asset concealment is far more common than simple paperwork errors; people often use complex offshore structures to hide assets or delay transfers simply because the structure is legally compliant. Specific \"invisible\" traps include vehicles held under family names other than the decedent's, inherited property kept in parents' names, or loans taken by trustees that are mistakenly valued at zero. These hidden items are frequently uncovered because the ISA filing requires a detailed memory statement detailing all property and money you own, forcing you to account for discrepancies when authorities spot unusual ownership gaps.",
