      "content": "Assets that are most prone to being lost include unregistered physical valuables like jewelry, art, or collectibles amassed in private homes or second homes abroad, which require long, detailed inventory statements to prove ownership. Even more dangerous are holdings in jurisdictions with no online registry, such as certain offshore islands or private jurisdictions, where the sole proof of title relies on a paper will and arbitrary ownership registries that many people mistakenly believe can bypass IHT rules. The \"invisible\" nature of these items often stems from an assumption that a handwritten will automatically covers them, whereas the law specifically requires proof of the asset's existence and valuation in every jurisdiction where the asset was held.",
